commit 402a42bc3877ea90095a89ecc123f98b29d9510e

C03: a declared folder field exempts the folder question from the machine-slot veto (FILES1441)

FILES1439 measured the current-directory count again: for the English variant the mind formulated «In which folder (Desktop, Documents, Downloads, or another) should the files be counted?», and the App's LooksLikeMachineSlotAsk rejected it («which folder» sits on its slot-ask list), then composed a question that never asks the folder.

Baxy.App UserMessagePolicy.ConversationReplyRejectionReason takes the mind's missing fields; AsksForDeclaredFolder exempts a question that names the folder or directory from the machine_slot_ask veto only when the mind declared folder as the missing field. MainWindowViewModel.AddMindClarification passes those fields. Every other veto stays. App recompiled (BUILD1441). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


